{
  "id": "b1-15",
  "level": "B1",
  "number": 15,
  "title": "Slang & culture: talk like a local",
  "titleAf": "Sleng en kultuur",
  "icon": "😎",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "b1-15-1",
      "title": "Everyday slang",
      "explanation": [
        "These words are everywhere in casual South African speech — and many are used in South African English too.",
        "**lekker** — great, nice. **Dit was lekker!**",
        "**kuier** — to visit/hang out (a core cultural word: relaxed time together). **Kom kuier by ons!**",
        "**ou** — guy (**die ouens** = the guys). **'n Goeie ou** = a good guy.",
        "**howzit** — hi, how's it going.",
        "**babbelas** — hangover. **dop** — a drink, or to fail a test.",
        "**bakkie** — pickup truck. **robot** — traffic light!"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Kom kuier Saterdag by ons!",
          "en": "Come hang out with us on Saturday!"
        },
        {
          "af": "Hy het die toets gedop.",
          "en": "He failed the test."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek het 'n babbelas.",
          "en": "I've got a hangover."
        },
        {
          "af": "Draai links by die robot.",
          "en": "Turn left at the traffic light."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "lekker",
        "kuier",
        "ou",
        "babbelas",
        "dop",
        "bakkie",
        "robot",
        "lus"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "In South Africa, a \"robot\" on the road is…",
          "options": [
            "a traffic light",
            "a speed camera",
            "a police officer"
          ],
          "answer": "a traffic light"
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "\"Hy het die toets gedop\" means…",
          "options": [
            "He passed the test",
            "He failed the test",
            "He drank at the test"
          ],
          "answer": "He failed the test"
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "en",
          "prompt": "Come visit us!",
          "answers": [
            "Kom kuier by ons!",
            "Kom kuier!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "af",
          "prompt": "Ek is lus vir 'n koffie.",
          "answers": [
            "I feel like a coffee.",
            "I feel like coffee.",
            "I'm in the mood for a coffee."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "fill",
          "af": "Ek het 'n ___ (hangover).",
          "en": "I've got a hangover.",
          "answers": [
            "babbelas"
          ],
          "options": [
            "babbelas",
            "bakkie",
            "braai"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-15-2",
      "title": "Little words with big flavour",
      "explanation": [
        "These small words are hard to translate but make you sound natural:",
        "**nou-nou** — in a moment (NOT \"right now\"!). **Ek kom nou-nou.**",
        "**sommer** — just, for no particular reason. **Ek het sommer gekom.**",
        "**mos** — you know, after all. **Ek het mos gesê!** (I told you so!)",
        "**darem** — at least, really. **Dit is darem mooi!**",
        "**ja-nee** — yes indeed (literally yes-no!).",
        "**foeitog** — aww, shame (sympathy). **eina** — ouch. **ag** — oh."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Ek kom nou-nou.",
          "en": "I'll be there in a moment."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek het mos gesê!",
          "en": "I told you so!"
        },
        {
          "af": "Ja-nee, dit is warm vandag.",
          "en": "Yes indeed, it's hot today."
        },
        {
          "af": "Foeitog, die arme hondjie!",
          "en": "Aww, the poor little dog!"
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "nou-nou",
        "sommer",
        "mos",
        "darem",
        "ja-nee",
        "eina",
        "ag"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "Your friend says \"Ek kom nou-nou.\" When will they arrive?",
          "options": [
            "Immediately",
            "In a little while",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": "In a little while"
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "You stub your toe. You say…",
          "options": [
            "Eina!",
            "Foeitog!",
            "Ja-nee!"
          ],
          "answer": "Eina!"
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "\"Ja-nee\" means…",
          "options": [
            "maybe",
            "yes indeed",
            "no"
          ],
          "answer": "yes indeed"
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "af",
          "prompt": "Ek het mos gesê!",
          "answers": [
            "I told you so!",
            "I did tell you!",
            "I said so!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-15-3",
      "title": "Terms of endearment & respect",
      "explanation": [
        "**skat**, **liefie**, **bokkie** — darling, sweetheart (partners, children).",
        "**Oom** and **Tannie** — respectful for any older man/woman. Using **jy** with an older stranger can sound rude; use **u** or Oom/Tannie.",
        "**boer maak 'n plan** — \"a farmer makes a plan\": the famous South African can-do attitude."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Dankie, Tannie!",
          "en": "Thank you, ma'am!"
        },
        {
          "af": "Moenie jou bekommer nie, boer maak 'n plan.",
          "en": "Don't worry, we'll find a way."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "skat",
        "liefie",
        "bokkie",
        "oom",
        "tannie",
        "boer maak 'n plan"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "You're thanking an older woman at a shop. Most respectful:",
          "options": [
            "Dankie, bokkie!",
            "Dankie, Tannie!",
            "Dankie, bru!"
          ],
          "answer": "Dankie, Tannie!"
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "\"Boer maak 'n plan\" means…",
          "options": [
            "Farmers plan their crops",
            "We'll find a way",
            "Make a farm plan"
          ],
          "answer": "We'll find a way"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
